# ForexConnect SDK — Linux x86_64 runtime-library provenance (companion to FCSDK.SHA256SUMS).
# vendor/fcsdk/linux is GITIGNORED (proprietary — never committed); this pins the .so set the
# Linux build/run path depends on, so a silently swapped SDK is detectable — the same guarantee the
# Windows FCSDK.SHA256SUMS gives the dll/lib/h layout. Kept as its own file (not folded into the
# sorted Windows manifest) so each stays self-consistent with its own regen command.
# SDK: ForexConnect 1.6.5 (built 2022-12-08). Versioned twins are byte-identical copies (same hash).
# Verified by crates/bridges/fxcm/scripts/provision-fcsdk.sh. Regenerate + re-verify on the dev box:
#   ( cd vendor/fcsdk/linux/lib && sha256sum *.so* ) | sort -k2 \
#     | sed 's#  #  fcsdk/linux/lib/#'
# A mismatch on refresh means the SDK changed — record WHY (new version, new download source).
